<h5>Pages</h5>
<p>Create static pages with title, slug, HTML body, optional <strong>visual layout builder</strong> (Section → Row → Column → Module), optional <strong>block builder</strong> (heading, paragraph, image, columns, CTA, spacer, custom HTML), draft/published status, optional <strong>parent page</strong> (hierarchy + breadcrumbs), and content width override. <strong>Public render order:</strong> visual layout → block builder → body. Open <strong>Edit via Frontend editor</strong> on an existing page to design the layout on a canvas that looks like the public site. On a row, use the <strong>Columns</strong> button or the side panel picker to choose 1–4 columns or common splits. Click <strong>+ Module</strong> (or an empty column) to pick a module type from the side panel — no browser prompts. Modules, rows, and sections can be reordered with ↑ ↓. Published pages are available at <code>/p/your-slug</code> or plain permalinks when configured. Use slug <code>welcome</code> or <code>home</code> as fallback homepage, or set the homepage under System → General → Reading.</p>
<p><strong>Inline media:</strong> Upload a featured/share image or block images directly on the page form (no need to visit Media first). New uploads appear in the Media library and get responsive sizes automatically.</p>
<p><strong>SEO &amp; social:</strong> SEO title, meta description (150–160 chars), featured share image (1200×630 recommended), optional <code>noindex</code>, and <strong>content width</strong> override (narrow / normal / wide) for the public page layout.</p>
<p><strong>LLM / AI:</strong> Plain-language summary for AI crawlers; JSON export at <code>/p/{slug}.json</code> or <code>/index.json</code> for homepage; Schema.org JSON-LD on public HTML; listed in <code>/llms.txt</code>.</p>
<p>Site-wide: <code>/sitemap.xml</code>, <code>/robots.txt</code>, <code>/llms.txt</code>, <code>/llms-full.txt</code>, <code>/site.json</code>, <code>/blog.json</code>. Set <code>base_url</code> in config for absolute social URLs.</p>
<p>Admin: <code>/admin/pages</code></p>
